			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:15:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1271,
				10
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement navigation history and label IPC handlers\n\nAdd a comprehensive suite of Wind IPC service handlers in `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/Navigation/` to bridge the Mountain backend with the editor's navigation state and labeling logic.\n\nThe implementation includes:\n- **History Management:** `HistoryPush`, `HistoryGoBack`, `HistoryGoForward`, `HistoryCanGoBack`, `HistoryCanGoForward`, `HistoryGetStack`, and `HistoryClear`. These handlers interact with `ApplicationRunTime.Environment.ApplicationState.Feature.NavigationHistory` to maintain the user's URI stack, enabling back/forward navigation and history views.\n- **Label Resolution:** `LabelGetBase`, `LabelGetURI`, and `LabelGetWorkspace`. These utility handlers compute display strings for tabs and breadcrumbs, supporting relative path resolution against the workspace root and extracting file basenames.\n\nAll handlers strictly adhere to the project's PascalCase naming convention, utilize the `ApplicationRunTime` environment for state access, and follow the modular 'one export per file' pattern. This completes the native backend support for the workbench's navigation UI.",
			"SHA": "2fde83158b1debd14ea02d3891b561b397d93c8c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
