				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement extension management IPC handlers\n\nAdd four new Wind IPC service handlers to `Source/IPC/WindServiceHandlers/Extensions/` to support extension lifecycle management and querying. The implementation includes:\n\n- `ExtensionsGet`: Fetches a single extension manifest by `<publisher>.<name>` identifier, returning `null` for missing entries to allow safe defaulting.\n- `ExtensionsGetAll`: Returns the full raw scan registry for debugging and tooling, bypassing `ILocalExtension` reshaping.\n- `ExtensionsGetInstalled`: The primary entry point for the UI, reshaping raw manifests into VS Code's `ILocalExtension` structure. This handler includes a 5-second polling mechanism to handle the boot-time race condition where the extension scanner populates data slightly after the workbench requests it, preventing the activity bar from losing extension icons. It also enforces type filtering (System vs. User) and injects safe defaults for missing `publisher`/`name`/`version` fields to prevent renderer crashes on `manifest` access.\n- `ExtensionsIsActive`: A predicate check confirming if an extension ID exists in the current registry.\n\nAll handlers strictly follow the project's PascalCase naming convention and modular 'one export per file' pattern, utilizing the `ApplicationRunTime` environment to interface with the `ExtensionManagementService`. The implementation preserves the distinction between raw scanner data and the workbench-shaped data required by the frontend.",
			"SHA": "4e5ce2c6d84be68562a02c4f999bd8090958f2a0"
		},
