				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Align FileSystem IPC handler with PascalCase invocation\n\nUpdate `FileStatNative` in the Wind IPC handler layer to strictly follow the project's PascalCase naming convention for method calls. Change invocations of `IsBenignEnoent` and `DebugOnce` from C-style function calls (`Function(...)`) to explicit method syntax (`Function::Fn(...)`). This ensures consistency with the recently modularized `DevLog` crate and the 'one export per file' pattern where utility functions are exposed as static methods on their respective structs.\n\nThe functional behavior for VFS logging gates remains unchanged, preserving the distinction between benign ENOENT errors and critical file access failures.",
			"SHA": "9002b742c990f181b8e56fc5c93940f52510df93"
		}
